     "user": "List 3DCP mortars from the literature whose static yield stress after 60 minutes of rest exceeds 10 kPa.",
     "text": "I’ll query the literature database, first checking its schema and then filtering 3DCP mortar records for static yield stress measured after 60 minutes of rest above 10 kPa.\nThe database contains 7 qualifying 3DCP mortar mixes from 2 papers:\n\n| Mix | Static yield stress at 60 min | w/b | s/b | Source confidence |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| 50S/50F | 40.00 kPa | 0.40 | 1.50 | Low |\n| 50S/35F/15G | 34.00 kPa | 0.40 | 1.50 | Low |\n| 50S/20F/30G | 21.00 kPa | 0.42 | 1.50 | Low |\n| 30% silica sand replacement | 19.86 kPa | 0.50 | 2.849 | High |\n| 20% silica sand replacement | 18.91 kPa | 0.50 | 2.896 | High |\n| 50S/0F/50G | 15.00 kPa | 0.42 | 1.50 | Low |\n| 10% silica sand replacement | 13.04 kPa | 0.50 | 2.951 | High |\n\nSources:\n\n- 50S-series mixes: “[Rheological, mechanical and fire resistance performance of waste glass activated geopolymers for concrete 3D printing](https://doi.org/10.1080/21650373.2025.2529994)” (2025).\n- Silica-sand-replacement mixes: “[Matric suction of fine aggregates and its contribution to the shape stability of 3D printed cementitious materials](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.conbuildmat.2022.127618)” (2022).\n\nThe 50S-series measurements have low extraction confidence; the silica-sand results are high-confidence table values. Full query output: `C:\\Users\\User\\3D Printing Concrete Prediction\\artifacts\\reports\\agent\\20261017-014039-836e\\sql_1792168865.csv`.\n",
